USOS CSMWrap patch 0017 (2026-10-18): SeaBIOS romfile-only options off

SeaBIOS built as a CSM has no romfile source: QEMU fw_cfg needs
CONFIG_QEMU_HARDWARE (off for CSM), CBFS needs CONFIG_COREBOOT_FLASH and
multiboot CONFIG_MULTIBOOT (both coreboot only); src/fw/csm.c adds only
"etc/extra-pci-roots-list". Three default-on features only act on a
romfile and are dead code in CSMWrap:
- CONFIG_BOOTSPLASH: "bootsplash.jpg"/"bootsplash.bmp" (jpeg.c, bmp.c and
  the splash half of bootsplash.c; the text console stays),
- CONFIG_SERCON: "etc/sercon-port" (the serial console in 16-bit code;
  INT 14h serial ports and the csmwrap.ini serial debug output stay),
- CONFIG_HOST_BIOS_GEOMETRY: "bios-geometry".
Turning them off frees ROM and F-segment space for later patches; the
behaviour on every machine is unchanged. Part of a MODIFIED CSMWrap made by
the USOS project (SeaBIOS LGPLv3).

diff -ruN a/seabios-config b/seabios-config
--- a/seabios-config
+++ b/seabios-config
@@ -3,3 +3,6 @@
 # CONFIG_VGAHOOKS is not set
 # CONFIG_TCGBIOS is not set
 CONFIG_VGA_COREBOOT=y
+# CONFIG_BOOTSPLASH is not set
+# CONFIG_SERCON is not set
+# CONFIG_HOST_BIOS_GEOMETRY is not set
